    {
      "title": "Bagoss Typeface System",
      "content": "Deel uses a proprietary 4-cut type family (BagossCondensedFont, BagossExtendedFont, BagossStandardFont, BagossStandardVF) as its typographic identity. Each cut has a defined role: Condensed at 44-60px for compressed hero headlines; Extended at 64px for wide-spread section banners; Standard at 12-16px for UI labels and badges; StandardVF for interactive elements (nav, buttons) where variable-font optical sizing matters. All cuts share ss01/ss02 OpenType features that enable stylistic alternate glyphs — these must remain active for authentic brand rendering. Do NOT substitute Bagoss with a condensed system font at headline sizes — the proportions are distinct enough to visually break the design. If Bagoss is unavailable, use Barlow Condensed (Google Fonts, weight 500) as a structural proxy while noting it lacks the custom OpenType personality."
